{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"better\": \"X\",\n  \"nets\": {\n    \"big\": \"X\",\n    \"small\": \"X\",\n    \"core\": \"平\",\n    \"concise\": \"Y\",\n    \"human\": \"X\",\n    \"fine\": \"X\",\n    \"load\": \"Y\"\n  },\n  \"why\": \"big：X 的大块直接交代人物此刻的状态、原因和变化，单扫大字也能串起故事；Y 的放大词虽然抓重点，但单独扫下来容易缺少因果和上下文。small：X 的感受更集中在人物当下的身体体验和心理反应，补充作用明确；Y 有不少内容转去描述左右手、声线和音型，和人物体验的连接稍弱。core：两版都完整呈现了亲近带来的幸福、对失去的恐惧以及最后接受不确定性，判平。concise：Y 的表达整体更紧凑，X 有些屏幕的大字和小字重复表达发酸、想留住当下、紧绷后松弛等意思。human：X 更自然；Y 有“像一句想了很久的话，到了嘴边先沉默几秒”的比喻悬空、“胸腔打开”“悲伤却进了幸福里面”“连这样待着都没了”等具体搭配或省略问题。fine：X 留下的体验更有辨识度，例如小船失重、温柔的刺、独处时泛酸、整理好衣服轻轻关门，更多是在讲观众能感受到什么；Y 有些感受被音乐本身的描述占据。load：Y 的放大词虽然数量不少，但每个都短；X 尤其 S11—S14 有多块较长的大字，单位时间内扫读压力更大。总体判 X，因为 X 在主线理解、感受补充、语言自然度和体验辨识度上占优，Y 的简洁和扫读优势不足以抵消这些差距。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "06afdda4-47e8-4854-8ec8-dd0955511aa3", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261110T193908035878Z", "elapsed_seconds": 248.312, "completed_utc": "2026-11-10T19:43:16.370174+00:00", "model": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "generation_policy_verified": true, "request_policy": {"model": "gpt-5-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "history_and_training_disabled": true, "temporary_chat_requests_personalization": false, "is_do_not_remember": false, "continuation": false, "unpersonalized_inherited_verified": false, "body_sha256": "e988bedcc930fc0302285e82ae275e09f1f6ec75c07b6fad58d52740b54435c4", "attachment_count": 0}, "stream_completion": {"sse_done": true, "message_completed": true, "independent_terminal_verified": true}, "profile": "Nozomi Kasaki / gpt4", "account_sha256": "bbd4fd636d4b6714d2b42b89e341bdb5bbe7c34f7d141aec76b444be8343fe54", "transport": "probridge-pure-http", "resume_requests": 0, "topic_connections": 0, "browser_started": false, "Docker_used": false, "automatic_retry": false, "initializer_pss_limit_mib": "not